    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Atmospheric dust modeling",
    "problem": "Projecting future U.S. dust activity is challenging because current climate models exhibit large uncertainty and struggle to accurately reproduce observed dust variability, making it unclear whether projected droughts will actually increase dust storms.",
    "method": "A multiple linear regression model is developed using satellite data to relate dust activity to precipitation, soil bareness, and wind speed, and is then used with climate model outputs to project future changes in American dustiness.",
    "task": "The task is to project future American dustiness in the late 21st century by applying projected changes in precipitation, soil bareness, and wind speed from CMIP5 models to a multiple linear regression model derived from recent satellite data.",
